---
<section id="privacy" class="section-sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto fade-in">
      <div class="card border-border/50">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="text-2xl mt-0.5">&#x1f512;</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-1">What "local" means, and what it doesn't</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary mb-4">
              OpenMind runs on your laptop with your own bCourses token. There is no OpenMind
              server, no account, and no telemetry &mdash; <span class="text-text-primary">but the AI is
              not local.</span>
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-2.5 text-xs mb-4">
              <div>
                <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Never leaves your machine:</span>
                <div class="text-text-secondary mt-1 space-y-0.5">
                  <div>&check; Your bCourses token &mdash; it lives in your OS keychain</div>
                  <div>&check; Your config and any indexed course materials (0600 files)</div>
                  <div>&check; Your conversations &mdash; OpenMind never sees them</div>
                  <div>&check; Nothing about your grades is ever written to disk</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Goes to your AI provider:</span>
                <div class="text-text-secondary mt-1 space-y-0.5">
                  <div>&bull; Whatever a tool returns &mdash; deadlines, grades, course text</div>
                  <div>&bull; Under Anthropic's or OpenAI's privacy policy, not ours</div>
                  <div>&bull; Only for the courses you chose at setup</div>
                  <div>&bull; If a course is sensitive, don't enable it</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-text-primary font-medium mb-1">Every place OpenMind connects to &mdash; four, and there is no fifth:</p>
            <div class="text-xs text-text-secondary space-y-0.5 mb-4">
              <div><code class="text-text-secondary">bcourses.berkeley.edu</code> &mdash; your courses, with your token</div>
              <div><code class="text-text-secondary">the file host bCourses redirects to</code> &mdash; only when reading a document, and the token is dropped first</div>
              <div><code class="text-text-secondary">github.com</code> &mdash; a public course-catalog file, once a day, nothing about you. Switch it off with <code class="text-text-secondary">data_updates=false</code></div>
              <div><code class="text-text-secondary">classes.berkeley.edu</code> &mdash; only when you ask whether a course is offered</div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary">
              There is no tool that can submit work, post a reply, send a message, or fetch an
              arbitrary URL &mdash; those routes don't exist in the code.
              <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind clear --all</code> deletes everything.
              <a href="https://github.com/qazybekb/openmind/blob/main/docs/PRIVACY.md" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">Full privacy documentation &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
